#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/docker.rst:2
msgid "Docker"
msgstr "Docker"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/docker.rst:4
msgid ""
"So far this document has covered how to add the VMware cloud integration "
"and has enabled users the ability to provision virtual machine based "
"instances via the `Add Instance` catalog in `Provisioning`. Another great"
" feature provided by |morpheus| out of the box is the ability to use "
"Docker containers and even support multiple containers per Docker host. "
"To do this a Docker Host must first be provisioned into VMware (multiple "
"are needed when dealing with horizontal scaling scenarios)."
msgstr ""
"So far este document tiene covered how to add el VMware cloud integration"
" y tiene habilitado users el ability to provision virtual machine based "
"instances via el `Add Instance` catalog in `Provisioning`. Another great "
"característica provided by |morpheus| out of el box es el ability to use "
"Docker containers y incluso support múltiples containers per Docker host."
" To do este un Docker Host debe primero be provisioned en VMware "
"(múltiples son needed cuando dealing con horizontal scaling scenarios)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/docker.rst:6
msgid ""
"To provision a Docker Host simply navigate to the Clusters tab of the "
"Cloud detail page or Infrastructure > Clusters section. From there, click"
" :guilabel:`+ ADD CLUSTER` to add a VMware Docker Host. This host will "
"show up in the Hosts tab next to other ESXi servers that were inventoried"
" by the VMware cloud integration. |morpheus| views a Docker host just "
"like any other Hypervisor with the caveat being that it is used for "
"running containerized images instead of virtualized ones. Once a Docker "
"Host is successfully provisioned a green checkmark will appear to the "
"right of the host marking it as available for use. In the event of a "
"failure click into the relevant host that failed and an error explaining "
"the failure will be displayed in red at the top."
msgstr ""
"To provision un Docker Host simply navigate to el Clusters pestaña of el "
"Cloud página de detalles o Infrastructure > Clusters sección. Desde elre,"
" click :guilabel:`+ AGREGAR CLUSTER` to add un VMware Docker Host. This "
"host será show up in el Hosts pestaña siguiente to otro ESXi servers que "
"fueron inventoried by el VMware cloud integration. |morpheus| views un "
"Docker host solo like cualquier otro Hypervisor con el caveat being que "
"it se utiliza para running containerized images en cambio of virtualized "
"ones. Once un Docker Host es successfully provisioned un green checkmark "
"será appear to el right of el host marking it as disponible para use. En "
"el evento of un failure click en el relevante host que fallido y un error"
" explaining el failure se mostrará in red en la parte superior."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/docker.rst:8
msgid ""
"The selected Docker layout may expose a configurable data volume. A "
"dedicated second disk is not required for every VMware Docker Host; "
"configure the volumes required by the selected layout and your storage "
"design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/docker.rst:10
msgid ""
"Some common error scenarios include network connectivity. For a Docker "
"Host to function properly, it must be able to resolve the |morpheus| "
"appliance url which can be configured in |AdmSet|. If it is unable to "
"resolve and negotiate with the appliance than the agent installation will"
" fail and provisioning instructions will not be able to be issued to the "
"host."
msgstr ""
"Some common error scenarios include network connectivity. For un Docker "
"Host to función properly, it debe be able to resolve el |morpheus| "
"appliance url cual se puede configurar in |AdmSet|. If it es unable to "
"resolve y negotiate con el appliance than el agente instalación será fail"
" y provisioning instructions no be able to be issued to el host."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/multitenancy.rst:2
msgid "Multitenancy"
msgstr "Multi-inquilino"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/multitenancy.rst:4
msgid ""
"A very common scenario for Managed Service Providers is the need to "
"provide access to VMware resources on a customer by customer basis. With "
"VMware several administrative features have been added to ensure customer"
" resources are properly scoped and isolated. For VMware it is possible to"
" assign specific `Networks`, `Datastores`, and `Resource Pools` to "
"customer accounts or even set the public visibility of certain resources,"
" therefore allowing all sub accounts access to the resource."
msgstr ""
"A muy common scenario para Managed Service Providers es el need to "
"provide acceso to VMware recursos on un customer by customer basis. With "
"VMware several administrative características tienen sido agregado to "
"ensure customer recursos son properly scoped y isolated. For VMware it es"
" possible to assign específico `Networks`, `Datastores`, y `Resource "
"Pools` to customer accounts o incluso set el público visibility of "
"certain recursos, por lo tanto allowing todos sub accounts acceso to el "
"recurso."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:2
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr "Advanced"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:4
msgid ""
"There are several advanced features provided within |morpheus| that can "
"leverage some cool aspects of VMware. One of these features is Remote "
"Console support directly to the hypervisor. To enable this feature a few "
"prerequisites must be met. First, the |morpheus| appliance must have "
"network access to the ESXi hosts within VCenter. Secondly, firewall "
"settings need to be adjusted on each ESXi host. This can be done in "
"VSphere under firewall configuration on the host. Simply check the "
"`gdbserver` option, which will open up the necessary ports (starting at "
"5900 range)."
msgstr ""
"There son several advanced características provided dentro de |morpheus| "
"que puede leverage algunos cool aspects of VMware. One of estos "
"características es Remote Console support directly to el hypervisor. To "
"enable este característica un few prerequisites debe be met. First, el "
"|morpheus| appliance debe tienen network acceso to el ESXi hosts dentro "
"de VCenter. Secondly, firewall configuración need to be adjusted on cada "
"ESXi host. This puede be done in VSphere under firewall configuración on "
"el host. Simply check el `gdbserver` opción, cual será open up el "
"necesario ports (starting at 5900 range)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:6
msgid "Hypervisor Console for vCenter 6.5 requires |morpheus| v3.2.0+"
msgstr "Hypervisor Console para vCenter 6.5 requires |morpheus| v3.2.0+"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:8
msgid ""
"Now that the ESXi hosts are ready to utilize remote console, simply edit "
"the cloud in |morpheus| via ``Infrastructure > Clouds``. Check the option"
" that says `Enable Hypervisor Console`. It is important to note that "
"currently this functionality only works for newly provisioned vm's "
"provisioned directly via |morpheus|. This should change soon however."
msgstr ""
"Now que el ESXi hosts son ready to utilize remoto console, simply edit la"
" nube in |morpheus| via ``Infrastructure > Clouds``. Marque la opción que"
" says `Enable Hypervisor Console`. It es importante to tenga en cuenta "
"que actualmente este functionality solo works para newly provisioned vm's"
" provisioned directly via |morpheus|. This debería cambio soon sin "
"embargo."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:10
msgid ""
"It is also possible to import vm snapshots for backup or conversion "
"purposes from VCenter and also an ESXi host. However, this does require "
"that the ESXi host license has an enterprise level license as it will not"
" allow the appliance to download a virtual image if it is not a paid "
"VMware license."
msgstr ""
"It es también possible to import vm snapshots para backup o conversion "
"purposes desde VCenter y también un ESXi host. Sin embargo, este does "
"require que el ESXi host license tiene un enterprise level license as it "
"no allow el appliance to download un virtual image if it no es un paid "
"VMware license."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:13
msgid "Device Type Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/advanced.rst:15
msgid ""
"The VMware Cloud advanced configuration contains separate "
":guilabel:`Enable Storage Type Selection` and :guilabel:`Enable Network "
"Type Selection` settings. Enable the applicable setting when users must "
"choose from the storage or network interface types exposed by the VMware "
"provisioning provider. When disabled, the corresponding selector is not "
"presented and the configured/default type is used. These settings are "
"verified for VMware Clouds only; do not infer the same controls for HVM "
"or another Cloud type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/permissions.rst:2
msgid "VMware Permissions"
msgstr "VMware Permissions"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/permissions.rst:4
msgid ""
"When integrating VMware vCenter with |morpheus|, users must supply "
"credentials for a vCenter account and |morpheus| will only have access "
"privileges equal to the integrated account. Many users will choose to use"
" a vCenter administrator account so that |morpheus| can freely do any "
"function in vCenter without worrying about hitting access limits. Others,"
" for security reasons, may want to restrict |morpheus| only to the "
"minimum permissions it needs to perform its functions. Follow the guide "
"in this section to configure a user with minimal permissions and "
"associate it with the appropriate usage levels before using it to create "
"a |morpheus| Cloud integration."
msgstr ""
"When integrating VMware vCenter con |morpheus|, users debe supply "
"credentials para un vCenter cuenta y |morpheus| será solo tienen acceso "
"privileges equal to el integrated cuenta. Many users será choose to use "
"un vCenter administrator cuenta so que |morpheus| puede freely do "
"cualquier función in vCenter sin worrying about hitting acceso limits. "
"Others, para security reasons, puede want to restrict |morpheus| solo to "
"el mínimo permisos it needs to perform its functions. Follow el guía en "
"esta sección to configure un usuario con minimal permisos y associate it "
"con el apropiado usage levels antes de using it to create un |morpheus| "
"Cloud integration."

